      "script": "Our property manager announced that maintenance requests only counted through the tenant portal. No calls, no texts, no hallway conversations. Then the portal went offline while water started dripping through my bathroom ceiling. I photographed every drop, recorded three unanswered calls, and emailed him anyway. He replied that without a portal ticket, there was no official problem. Fine. When the site returned, I submitted one request containing the photos, call log, his email, and a timestamped video of the ceiling collapsing into the tub. The insurance adjuster arrived the next morning and asked why nobody responded sooner. The manager tried blaming me for waiting. I opened the ticket on my phone and showed the adjuster his written refusal. The building paid for my hotel, the bathroom, and damage downstairs. A week later, the new policy said emergencies should be reported by any available method. Apparently water can read the portal rules, but it chose not to comply.",
